<h2 id="bottom-line">Bottom Line</h2>

<p>Amazon has moved the Kindle Oasis onto its stricter KFX-ZIP encryption, and most DRM-removal tools no longer work on the books it downloads. The Kindle Voyage is now the last supported Amazon reader without the new scheme — a narrow window for anyone who still wants tool-friendly copies of purchases.</p>

<p>For readers who own their libraries as EPUB files, nothing changes: a local EPUB is beyond the reach of any Amazon update. If you are affected, the constructive response is the same one we recommend for every shift in the ebook ecosystem — move the books you care about into EPUB while you can, back them up under your control, and read on whichever device fits today. That is the only library no firmware update can touch.</p>
